    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"dimension\",\n  \"unit\": null,\n  \"additive_over_entities\": null,\n  \"additive_over_time\": null,\n  \"time_rollup\": null,\n  \"valid_methods\": [],\n  \"period_basis\": \"mixed\",\n  \"derivation\": null,\n  \"calendar\": null,\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": null,\n  \"annualized\": null,\n  \"entity_grain\": null,\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": null,\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"source\": \"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts\",\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\",\n    \"retrieved_on\": \"2026-10-24\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Categorical label for the reporting period a fundamentals value covers. Five distinct values appear: FY (full fiscal year), Q (single fiscal quarter), YTD6 (cumulative first six months of the fiscal year), YTD9 (cumulative first nine months), and instant (a point-in-time balance). YTD6 and YTD9 values are cumulative and overlap with Q and FY rows, so rows with different period_basis values should not be summed together. Fiscal period boundaries vary by company, for example WING and DRI use 52/53-week fiscal calendars. Use this column to filter or group rows before aggregating the value column.\"\n}",
